message.content:
Zimmermann PWA Kit, SFCC-236 product card. Real bug found via live browser testing on the composed `Commerce/ZimmProductCard` Storybook story: hovering the card reveals the carousel arrows correctly and paging through images works, but moving the mouse OUT of the card does not hide the arrows again — they stay visible until the user clicks somewhere outside the card entirely.

Root cause (confirmed by reading the recipe + an empirical jsdom probe, not guessed): `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/zimmProductCard.css.ts`'s `root` part reveals the carousel (and, identically, price/the size-selector/notify-me) via a `&:hover`/`&:focus-within` pair scoped to the whole card root. Clicking an arrow button gives it real DOM focus in every evergreen browser engine, so `:focus-within` on the card root stays `true` after the mouse leaves — the reveal rule never turns back off until focus moves elsewhere (e.g. a click outside the card). This is not unique to the carousel: every one of this file's `:focus-within`-based reveals (price show, price hide, size-selector reveal, notify-me reveal) shares the exact same shared-root mechanism and the exact same latent bug — clicking a size chip or the notify-me button would reproduce the identical stuck-open symptom. User confirmed (via an explicit scope question) that ALL FIVE occurrences should be fixed together, not just the carousel one that was reported.

The fix: replace `:focus-within` with `:has(:focus-visible)` everywhere in this recipe. `:focus-visible` only matches when the browser's own heuristic says a *keyboard*-triggered focus ring is warranted — a mouse-click-focused `<button>` does not satisfy it in any evergreen engine, but genuine Tab navigation still does. So keyboard parity (the reason a focus-based reveal exists at all — `display:none` removes an element from tab order, so `:hover` alone would make it permanently unreachable by keyboard) is fully preserved, while the mouse-click-stays-open bug is not.

`:has()` is not used anywhere else in this codebase yet — this is the first use. It is fully covered by this project's own `browserslist` in `package.json` (`iOS >= 17`, `Android >= 14`, `last 4 ChromeAndroid versions`), all far past `:has()`'s 2022/2023 shipping baseline, so no further support check is needed. Confirmed via an empirical jsdom probe (run and deleted, not left behind) that this project's jsdom (nwsapi-backed) supports `:has()` and treats `:focus-visible` as satisfied by any `.focus()` call — so existing/updated unit tests using `.focus()` + `.matches()` will still pass. jsdom has no concept of "focus caused by a mouse click" vs "focus caused by Tab" (there is no such distinction to probe), so — same shape as this file's own pre-existing "KNOWN LIMITATION" note about jsdom not resolving stacking contexts (see `index.test.tsx`'s Fix 3 section) — a unit test can prove the reveal still fires on real focus, but only a real browser can prove the mouse-click case is excluded. Say so explicitly in the new test comment, don't imply full coverage.

The next available lettered "Fix" label in this file's own sequence (C, D, E, F, G already used) is **Fix H**. Use that label everywhere below.

## 1. `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/zimmProductCard.css.ts`

Five token-level selector changes, each changing the string `&:focus-within ` to `&:has(:focus-visible) ` inside the existing template-literal keys (nothing else about the key or its value changes) — these five, identified by the `CARD_SLOT` they target:
- `CARD_SLOT.price` in the `hoverRevealsPrice` block (the `display: 'block'` one)
- `CARD_SLOT.price` in the `hoverHidesPrice` block (the `display: 'none'` one)
- `CARD_SLOT.sizeChips` in the `hoverRevealsSizeSelector` block
- `CARD_SLOT.notifyMe` in the `hoverRevealsNotifyMe` block
- `CARD_SLOT.carousel` at the end (the arrows reveal)

Plus these exact doc/comment rewrites (find each block by its current text below, replace with the new text — preserve surrounding code/indentation exactly, only the comment prose and the one selector token per block change):

a) Module docblock point 3 (currently ends "`:hover` OR `:focus-within` on this same root (Fix 2 rework below) — `:hover`...") — change to:
```
 *   3. THE HOVER-REVEAL SWAP between price and the PLP/Wishlist size-selector (and Home's
 *      hidden-by-default price), gated by the same `(hover: hover) and (pointer: fine)` query
 *      `zimmProductCardMedia.css.ts` already uses for its own arrows/indicator split. Each reveal
 *      rule fires on `:hover` OR `:has(:focus-visible)` on this same root (Fix 2 rework below,
 *      superseded by Fix H — see point 6) — `:hover` alone would leave every reveal permanently
 *      unreachable by keyboard on a hover-capable device, since `display: none` removes the
 *      unconditional-state element from the tab order entirely and nothing but a real pointer
 *      hover could ever have revealed it.
```

b) Module docblock point 6 — the paragraph currently ends "...the `:hover`/`:focus-within` pair here is the only reveal path left, the same mechanism point 3 already established for price/the size-selector. Purely additive to the existing `carousel` z-index lift in point 2 above — that lift already handles stacking once the arrows are visible; this handles visibility itself." Change `:focus-within` in that sentence to `:has(:focus-visible)`, then append this new paragraph directly after it (still inside the same docblock, same `*` prefix style):
```
 *
 *      Fix H (live-browser check immediately after the above shipped): clicking an arrow button
 *      gives it real DOM focus in every evergreen engine, which kept the then-`:focus-within`
 *      reveal true — and the arrows visible — even after the mouse moved back out, until focus
 *      moved elsewhere entirely (confirmed live: arrows stayed up until a click landed outside
 *      the card). The same shared-root `:focus-within` shape underlies every reveal in point 3
 *      too (price, the size-selector, notify-me), so a click on a size chip or the notify-me
 *      button reproduces the identical stuck-open symptom — this fix was therefore applied to
 *      every `:focus-within` occurrence in this recipe, not just this one. `:has(:focus-visible)`
 *      replaces `:focus-within` everywhere in this file: it matches only when the browser's own
 *      heuristic says a keyboard focus ring is warranted, which a mouse-click-focused `<button>`
 *      never satisfies in any evergreen engine, while genuine Tab navigation still does — so
 *      keyboard parity (Fix 2's original reason for adding a focus-based reveal at all) is fully
 *      preserved, and the mouse-click case is not. `:has()` is new to this codebase as of this
 *      fix; it is fully covered by this project's own browserslist (`iOS >= 17`, `Android >= 14`,
 *      `last 4 ChromeAndroid versions`), all far past `:has()`'s 2022/2023 shipping baseline.
```

c) The big inline comment directly above the `hoverRevealsPrice` block's focus rule (currently starts "// Fix 2 (Scorer rework round 1): `display: none` removes an element from the tab" and ends "...because the descendant-combinator path has to be baked into the selector itself.") — replace the whole comment with:
```
          // Fix 2 (Scorer rework round 1): `display: none` removes an element from the tab
          // order entirely, so a keyboard-only user on a hover-capable device (tabbing, not
          // hovering) could never reveal this via `:hover` alone. Originally `:focus-within` on
          // this same root — scoped here, not on the price/size-chip wrapper itself, so that
          // focus landing on ANY descendant control (name link, bag button, size chip) triggers
          // the reveal — mirroring zimmSearchInput.css.ts's container/zimmFormRow's own
          // `_focusWithin` sibling to `_hover`.
          // Fix H (live-browser check after the arrow reveal shipped): plain `:focus-within`
          // does not distinguish a real Tab-focused descendant from one that only has focus
          // because the user *clicked* it with a mouse — most browsers give a `<button>` real
          // DOM focus on click, so clicking any interactive control inside the card (an arrow,
          // a size chip, notify-me) left `:focus-within` true, and therefore every reveal below
          // stuck open, until focus moved elsewhere entirely (e.g. a click outside the card) —
          // moving the mouse back out was not enough. `:has(:focus-visible)` fixes this: it only
          // matches when the browser's own focus-visible heuristic says a *keyboard* focus ring
          // is warranted, which excludes a mouse-click-focused `<button>` in every evergreen
          // engine but still matches genuine Tab navigation — so the keyboard case Fix 2 exists
          // for keeps working, and the mouse-click case that produced the stuck-open bug does
          // not. `:has()` is not used anywhere else in this codebase yet; it is fully covered by
          // this project's own browserslist (`iOS >= 17`, `Android >= 14`, `last 4 ChromeAndroid
          // versions`), all far past `:has()`'s 2022/2023 shipping baseline. Expressed as a
          // separate string key (not a comma-joined `'&:hover, &:has(:focus-visible) ...'`
          // selector) to match this file's own established idiom; raw selector strings are used
          // throughout rather than a Chakra shorthand prop because the descendant-combinator
          // path has to be baked into the selector itself, and Chakra has no `:has()` shorthand.
```

d) The `hoverHidesPrice` block's focus-rule comment (currently "// Fix 2 — see the hoverRevealsPrice block above for the full rationale. Keyboard focus / // anywhere in the card must hide price in favour of the size-selector exactly as hover / // does, so a keyboard user sees the identical revealed state, not a different partial / // one.") — replace with:
```
          // Fix 2 / Fix H — see the hoverRevealsPrice block above for the full rationale.
          // Keyboard focus anywhere in the card must hide price in favour of the size-selector
          // exactly as hover does, so a keyboard user sees the identical revealed state, not a
          // different partial one; `:has(:focus-visible)` keeps that true while no longer
          // sticking open after a mouse click.
```

e) The `hoverRevealsSizeSelector` block's one-line comment ("// Fix 2 — see the hoverRevealsPrice block above for the full rationale.") — replace with:
```
          // Fix 2 / Fix H — see the hoverRevealsPrice block above for the full rationale.
```

f) In the `hoverRevealsNotifyMe` block, there is currently no comment directly above its focus-rule line — add one directly above it:
```
          // Fix 2 / Fix H — see the hoverRevealsPrice block above for the full rationale.
```

## 2. `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/index.test.tsx`

- Rename every constant whose name starts `FOCUS_WITHIN_` to start `FOCUS_VISIBLE_` instead (e.g. `FOCUS_WITHIN_CAROUSEL_KEY` → `FOCUS_VISIBLE_CAROUSEL_KEY`, and likewise for `_PRICE_KEY`, `_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY`, `_NOTIFY_ME_KEY`), and update every usage site of each renamed constant throughout the file accordingly.
- In each renamed constant's own definition, change the template-string value from `` `&:focus-within ${...}` `` to `` `&:has(:focus-visible) ${...}` ``.
- Update the inline comment immediately above the `FOCUS_WITHIN_PRICE_KEY`/`FOCUS_WITHIN_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY`/`FOCUS_WITHIN_NOTIFY_ME_KEY` definitions (currently explaining "the equivalent here is a separate `'&:focus-within ...'` string key alongside the existing `'&:hover ...'` key, not a merged `'&:hover, &:focus-within ...'`") — change both `:focus-within` mentions in that comment to `:has(:focus-visible)`.
- Test names/descriptions that say "focus-within" (e.g. `'carousel arrows: unconditional hover+focus-within reveal...'`, `'...both swap on hover AND on focus-within'`, `'...no hover-reveal or focus-within-reveal rule is emitted...'`) — change "focus-within" to "focus-visible" in each.
- The real-DOM proof test block (its own docblock starts "Fix 2 (Scorer rework round 1) — DOM-level proof that the `:focus-within` reveal genuinely..." and the test itself is titled `'an ancestor :focus-within + the real recipe's own descendant-selector suffix flips from non-matching to matching once a nested control receives real focus'`):
  - Retitle the test to `'an ancestor :has(:focus-visible) + the real recipe's own descendant-selector suffix flips from non-matching to matching once a nested control receives real focus'`.
  - Update the docblock/comments in this block to describe `:has(:focus-visible)` instead of `:focus-within` (same "DOM-level proof it genuinely matches" framing, updated pseudo-class name and any selector-string mentions like `element.matches(':focus-within')` → `element.matches(':has(:focus-visible)')`).
  - It will use the renamed `FOCUS_VISIBLE_SIZE_CHIPS_KEY` constant (already renamed above) — no other logic change needed, since `.focus()` in jsdom satisfies `:focus-visible` the same way it satisfied `:focus-within` (confirmed empirically before this dispatch).
  - Add one new sentence to this block's comment, in the same voice as this file's own pre-existing "KNOWN LIMITATION" note (see the Fix 3 describe block elsewhere in this file for that established pattern/wording style) — something to this effect: jsdom has no concept of "focus triggered by a mouse click" vs "focus triggered by keyboard," so this test proves the reveal still fires on real focus, exactly as it did for `:focus-within` — it cannot prove (only a real browser can) that a mouse-click-focused button is excluded, which is the actual bug this fix addresses.
  - Run this file's test suite after making these changes and confirm every test still passes — do not just assume the rename was mechanical; actually run `npx vitest run overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/index.test.tsx`.

## 3. `overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/index.tsx`

Two comment-only mentions of "focus-within" (lines ~49 and ~428, both casual phrasing like "hover/focus-within" describing the general behaviour, not a selector literal) — change "focus-within" to "focus-visible" in both.

## After making all changes

Run, from the repo root:
- `npx tsc --noEmit`
- `npx vitest run overrides/app/components/ui-kits/organisms/zimmProductCard/`

Both must be clean. Do not touch `zimmProductCardMedia.css.ts`, `zimmProductCardMedia/index.tsx`, or any other file — this step is scoped to exactly the three files named above. Do not run `git add` or commit anything; report back what you changed and the exact tsc/vitest output.

